      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitamity.org/about_1/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Brothers Joseph and Ahio S. Watt founded Amity between 1848 and 1849 after immigrating over the Oregon Trail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amity%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Amity was named after a school built by two rival communities following the amicable settlement of a dispute.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amity%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Joseph Watt established the first woolen mill in Oregon and was the first to ship Oregon wheat to England.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
